WEBVTT

00:00.770 --> 00:02.770
At the dawn of the Seika era,

00:02.770 --> 00:06.010
in order to regulate unwanted messages that presented a bad influence to society,

00:06.010 --> 00:08.280
the Media Cleansing Act was passed.

00:09.460 --> 00:12.820
The libraries armed themselves in order to protect freedom of expression

00:12.820 --> 00:15.120
from the extreme censorship of the Media Cleansing Committee.

00:15.910 --> 00:19.120
The conflict between the two continued to escalate.

00:20.240 --> 00:25.540
In the 31st year of Seika, a lone girl plunged herself into the middle of that conflict.

00:33.030 --> 00:37.630
usu murasaki hirogaru

00:33.030 --> 00:37.630
The faint purple spreads across the sky

00:37.630 --> 00:45.610
orenji iro ni kawaru mado no soto

00:37.630 --> 00:45.610
The color changes to orange outside the window

00:45.610 --> 00:49.660
yoru wa mou bai bai

00:45.610 --> 00:49.660
The night's already "bye-bye"

00:50.210 --> 00:55.900
tada kirei na mono wo kirei to

00:50.210 --> 00:55.900
I just want to be someone who

00:55.900 --> 01:00.460
ieru atashi de itai

00:55.900 --> 01:00.460
calls beautiful things beautiful

01:00.460 --> 01:06.800
ima wa dokidoki shitai no

01:00.460 --> 01:06.800
I want to get excited for it!

01:07.330 --> 01:11.860
fumidashichae tomaranai

01:07.330 --> 01:11.860
So I step out, unstoppable

01:11.860 --> 01:16.450
zenbu te ni hairi sou de

01:11.860 --> 01:16.450
And take everything into my own hands

01:16.940 --> 01:21.050
sono saki de aitai

01:16.940 --> 01:21.050
Beyond there, I want to meet

01:21.050 --> 01:27.040
mita koto no nai atashi

01:21.050 --> 01:27.040
the new self that I've never seen

01:27.510 --> 01:32.160
sayonara daisuki na machi

01:27.510 --> 01:32.160
Farewell, my beloved town

01:32.160 --> 01:36.710
atashi mo ganbatte miru yo

01:32.160 --> 01:36.710
I'll try to do my best

01:36.710 --> 01:44.270
kono sora no tsuzuku basho de

01:36.710 --> 01:44.270
somewhere under the same sky

01:47.290 --> 01:50.510
I idolized the prince I met when I was in high school.

01:50.510 --> 01:54.620
Now, I, Kasahara Iku, am working in a library like I've always dreamed of.

01:55.020 --> 01:59.070
I was assigned to the hyper elite special book forces

01:59.070 --> 02:01.610
known as the Library Task Force.

02:00.080 --> 02:00.710
NOTICE

02:00.080 --> 02:00.710
KASAHARA IKU

02:00.870 --> 02:01.500
YOU ARE TO REPORT TO

02:01.610 --> 02:04.640
Will I be all right?!

02:01.670 --> 02:02.560
THE LIBRARY TASK FORCE

02:07.910 --> 02:12.360
Situation 02

02:07.910 --> 02:12.360
Library Task Force

02:20.440 --> 02:21.550
What do you think?

02:21.550 --> 02:26.480
Doesn't training in the green richness of nature feel great?

02:22.010 --> 02:24.670
Genda Ryusuke

02:22.070 --> 02:23.070
Defence Force, Captain of Task Force

02:23.070 --> 02:24.000
Rank: Library Supervisor Third Class

02:24.000 --> 02:24.670
Middle Aged Wrangler

02:25.730 --> 02:28.580
Kasahara Iku

02:25.790 --> 02:26.790
Defence Force, Library Task Force

02:26.480 --> 02:29.350
It's too green and rich.

02:26.790 --> 02:27.720
Rank: Librarian First Class

02:27.720 --> 02:28.580
Hot-headed Idiot

02:30.930 --> 02:31.560
Sorry!

02:31.680 --> 02:34.000
Tezuka Hikaru

02:31.740 --> 02:32.740
Defence Force, Library Task Force

02:32.740 --> 02:33.670
Rank: Librarian First Class

02:33.670 --> 02:34.000
Stubborn Young Man

02:35.500 --> 02:37.980
What's wrong with him?!

02:38.230 --> 02:41.020
Librarian First Class Tezuka Hikaru.

02:41.020 --> 02:43.070
Librarian First Class Kasahara Iku.

02:43.570 --> 02:50.340
As of June 25th of the 31st year of Seika, you have been reassigned to the Library Task Force.

02:50.340 --> 02:51.740
Thank you, Sir.

02:51.740 --> 02:57.390
The recommendations came from Library Supervisor Third Class Genda Ryusuke, the Captain of the Task Force,

02:57.890 --> 03:03.500
and Task Force Library Officers Second Class Komaki Mikihisa and Dojo Atsushi.

03:04.900 --> 03:08.570
I realized the faults in my teaching during that incident the other day.

03:08.570 --> 03:12.510
From now on, I will retrain you very hard, so be prepared.

03:14.680 --> 03:16.150
Special training?

03:16.150 --> 03:20.000
Yeah. It will double as orientation.

03:16.800 --> 03:19.660
Shibasaki Asako

03:16.810 --> 03:18.000
Defence Force, Library Task Force

03:18.000 --> 03:19.010
Rank: Librarian First Class

03:19.010 --> 03:19.660
Informant

03:20.000 --> 03:22.570
So you'll be with Tezuka.

03:22.570 --> 03:24.400
You know Tezuka?

03:24.970 --> 03:26.740
More than just know him.

03:26.740 --> 03:29.630
He was always the best in basic training.

03:29.630 --> 03:33.380
He's an especially skilled recruit amongst this year's rookies.

03:33.840 --> 03:37.160
Is he really that great?

03:37.160 --> 03:41.630
What was up with that spiteful glare just now anyway?!

03:42.450 --> 03:47.360
Hey, newcomer, if you have any complaints, state them clearly.

03:47.360 --> 03:50.410
No, I... uh...

03:50.410 --> 03:53.130
I thought the library force mainly operated in the inner city, right?

03:53.130 --> 03:58.510
So I was wondering why we have to do our training so far away from the city.

03:59.170 --> 04:00.150
For the mood.

04:01.900 --> 04:04.930
It's to prepare ourselves for the Hino Nightmare.

04:04.930 --> 04:06.570
The Hino Nightmare?

04:06.570 --> 04:08.400
Didn't you...?

04:06.670 --> 04:09.530
Dojo Atsushi

04:06.680 --> 04:07.870
Defence Force, Library Task Force

04:07.870 --> 04:08.880
Rank: Library Officer Second Class

04:08.880 --> 04:09.530
Angry Shorty

04:10.200 --> 04:12.370
Of course not.

04:12.370 --> 04:14.330
I know Hino Library!

04:14.330 --> 04:17.080
Don't brag about knowing that library!

04:17.080 --> 04:17.760
I'm not.

04:17.760 --> 04:19.550
I said it because I knew it, that's all.

04:19.550 --> 04:22.210
Is that how you should behave towards the one who's training you?!

04:22.210 --> 04:26.300
The Hino Nightmare is the incident in which a group siding with the Media Cleansing Committee

04:26.300 --> 04:32.760
raided the Hino City Library on February 7th of the 11th year of Seika.

04:32.760 --> 04:36.300
The library forces were not well organized back then,

04:36.300 --> 04:38.630
so the coordination with the neighboring forces was delayed,

04:38.630 --> 04:42.960
and it evolved into a major disaster with 12 casualties on the Hino Library's side.

04:42.960 --> 04:45.420
It's the incident that set about the formation of library forces in the 10 regions,

04:45.420 --> 04:48.280
and the current system of library forces.

04:48.280 --> 04:51.280
As expected from Tezuka.

04:51.280 --> 04:59.000
I can't believe how someone who doesn't know this can be in the Task Force.

05:00.410 --> 05:02.160
I take my words back.

05:02.830 --> 05:07.060
There are reasons why Kasahara was chosen as well.

05:07.060 --> 05:10.470
It is not something you can judge by your standards.

05:10.470 --> 05:14.470
Did he just defend me?

05:24.980 --> 05:28.010
Half of them barely hit the target.

05:28.010 --> 05:30.240
I'm really trying to aim straight...

05:30.240 --> 05:34.070
You'll need to be able to hit the target every time.

05:30.500 --> 05:33.800
Komaki Mikihisa

05:30.510 --> 05:31.700
Defence Force, Library Task Force

05:31.700 --> 05:32.710
Rank: Library Officer Second Class

05:32.710 --> 05:33.800
Smiling Logican

05:36.830 --> 05:39.950
LFC Tezuka is impressive after all.

05:39.950 --> 05:44.500
These things are to be expected of a person who was chosen to join the Task Force.

05:44.490 --> 05:47.240
Show off...

05:45.180 --> 05:47.250
What a show-off!

05:55.890 --> 05:59.100
Fuel is not cheap either, so let's keep up the pace!

06:02.480 --> 06:04.480
Kasahara, coming down!

06:09.270 --> 06:10.560
That was perfect.

06:10.560 --> 06:12.120
Very impressive.

06:12.730 --> 06:15.190
You're casually praising me...?

06:15.190 --> 06:17.410
Rare things do happen...

06:17.410 --> 06:19.950
I gave you the evaluation that you deserve.

06:19.950 --> 06:21.710
That's all.

06:21.710 --> 06:23.840
Accept that evaluation.

06:23.840 --> 06:26.420
It doesn't happen very often for you.

06:29.820 --> 06:31.050
What's the matter, Tezuka?

06:31.050 --> 06:33.760
Oh, nothing.

06:33.760 --> 06:35.180
Tezuka is up next.

06:35.180 --> 06:36.510
Let's check him out.

06:51.380 --> 06:56.610
Could it be that Tezuka is afraid of heights?

06:58.100 --> 07:02.030
The last item of this training camp is hiking.

07:02.030 --> 07:05.700
Split into two teams, and head to the destination using a compass as your guide.

07:05.700 --> 07:07.540
Go!

07:07.540 --> 07:14.830
Many tree farmers have reported bear sightings, so stay on the alert.

07:16.510 --> 07:18.760
B-Bears?!

07:18.760 --> 07:21.300
You're to deal with them on your own.

07:21.300 --> 07:22.350
That'll be all.

07:24.280 --> 07:26.980
Wait... On our own?

07:27.620 --> 07:31.640
As far as I know, no bears have been sighted during hiking.

07:31.640 --> 07:34.850
But they might appear this time!

07:34.850 --> 07:38.560
Rather than worrying about whether or not bears will appear,

07:38.560 --> 07:40.450
worry about your stamina.

07:42.490 --> 07:44.380
But we're talking about bears!

07:44.380 --> 07:49.370
The only person who could face a bear head on is Captain Genda!

07:58.340 --> 07:59.820
What is this...?

07:59.820 --> 08:02.350
It's harder than I expected.

08:02.350 --> 08:05.310
Tezuka, carry Kasahara's spade.

08:06.650 --> 08:11.370
In group activities, it's not a matter of succeeding by finishing on your own.

08:11.370 --> 08:12.730
Roger.

08:12.730 --> 08:14.420
I'm fine!

08:14.420 --> 08:15.730
I can do it—

08:14.730 --> 08:17.750
Don't make me repeat myself, Kasahara.

08:21.100 --> 08:23.620
So, you got here within a day.

08:23.620 --> 08:26.830
You did well, despite having a female member on your team.

08:26.830 --> 08:31.170
I need to use the toilet, so please don't come this way.

08:32.880 --> 08:36.130
I don't even hesitate to do stuff like this anymore.

08:36.130 --> 08:40.090
My parents might die of shock if they found out.

09:04.780 --> 09:06.240
A bear?!

09:16.090 --> 09:17.250
Are you serious?!

09:17.250 --> 09:19.960
So you punched the bear?!

09:21.380 --> 09:26.510
But it was one of my superiors in a bear costume!

09:26.510 --> 09:29.580
But you punched him, thinking he was a bear, right?

09:29.580 --> 09:33.630
No girl, no human would do that...

09:33.630 --> 09:35.480
It wasn't just me!

09:36.340 --> 09:39.440
I didn't expect a second generation Dojo to appear.

09:39.440 --> 09:42.900
She really resembles you in your newcomer days.

09:44.170 --> 09:45.460
Good morning.

09:45.460 --> 09:47.910
Hello, Bear Slayer Kasahara.

09:48.560 --> 09:52.600
I got all kinds of nicknames because of you, Instructor Dojo.

09:52.600 --> 09:57.630
I told you that no bears have ever been sighted during hiking!

09:57.630 --> 10:02.980
It's unreasonable to expect us to realize that it's an annual prank played on the rookies just from that!

10:02.980 --> 10:04.770
Tezuka realized it!

10:04.770 --> 10:06.590
Yes, I'm an idiot!

10:06.590 --> 10:09.160
I advised them a bunch of times that we shouldn't do it!

10:09.160 --> 10:11.920
So it's all my fault?!

10:11.920 --> 10:14.540
You're so full of energy first thing in the morning,

10:14.540 --> 10:17.020
Bear Slayers.

10:17.610 --> 10:20.030
Kasahara, we have a new request.

10:20.030 --> 10:21.090
Yes!

10:21.090 --> 10:23.660
Kasahara-san, what about the request from earlier?

10:23.660 --> 10:25.320
I'm sorry, I don't have it yet.

10:25.320 --> 10:29.280
Sorry, Tezuka, but what rack is 756 in?

10:29.280 --> 10:31.750
Craft works shelf in the 30's!

10:31.750 --> 10:33.460
Will you cut that out?!

10:33.460 --> 10:34.750
You <i>just</i> asked me about crafts!

10:34.750 --> 10:36.450
Kasahara!

10:36.450 --> 10:37.900
Y-Yes!

10:41.180 --> 10:42.870
Are you an idiot?!

10:45.180 --> 10:46.850
This was sent back.

10:46.850 --> 10:49.640
The search was too slow and the user couldn't wait any longer.

10:49.640 --> 10:51.660
I'm sorry.

10:51.660 --> 10:54.200
There are complaints from the main check-out desk, too.

10:54.200 --> 10:55.620
We should think about what to do.

10:57.160 --> 10:59.100
It's all your fault.

10:59.700 --> 11:02.900
What's up with a Task Force member who can't even categorize books?

11:02.900 --> 11:08.910
Why didn't you study the basics when you were fully aware that library training was coming up?!

11:09.380 --> 11:14.170
But the training started right after camp.

11:14.170 --> 11:16.080
There was a day off in between!

11:16.080 --> 11:19.930
Couldn't you have studied the categories then?!

11:19.930 --> 11:22.750
And you don't remember the rack placements no matter how many times I tell you.

11:22.750 --> 11:26.760
Idiots who have no skill and make no effort are the worst!

11:27.330 --> 11:30.720
You hold me back all the time, and you even talk back to me.

11:30.720 --> 11:33.470
Incompetent people like you shouldn't talk!

11:34.180 --> 11:35.160
Tezuka!

11:35.160 --> 11:36.580
You said too much.

11:36.580 --> 11:39.960
You can't say whatever you want just because you're right.

11:39.960 --> 11:44.610
It's a little early, but let's ask for requests from other libraries.

11:44.610 --> 11:46.390
Kasahara, you take care of them.

11:47.880 --> 11:48.910
Yes, Sir.

11:57.080 --> 12:00.540
539, 539...

12:02.540 --> 12:04.500
Finally done.

12:04.500 --> 12:06.880
It was hectic like a war today.

12:09.110 --> 12:11.300
I'll stay a little longer.

12:11.300 --> 12:12.630
I see.

12:12.630 --> 12:15.560
If that's the case, lock the book vault before you leave.

12:15.560 --> 12:16.600
Yes, Sir.

12:37.190 --> 12:39.130
I brought some refreshments.

12:39.130 --> 12:41.710
Do you want to have them with me when you have some time?

12:41.710 --> 12:43.290
Shibasaki...

12:43.290 --> 12:43.920
Why?

12:43.920 --> 12:47.940
Instructor Dojo asked me to come and check on you.

12:47.940 --> 12:51.430
Geez, he's so easy on you.

12:54.770 --> 12:57.100
Shibasaki, I have a favor to ask of you.

12:57.100 --> 12:59.650
Can you teach me some library work?

13:00.900 --> 13:02.810
I knew you'd ask that.

13:04.080 --> 13:06.220
It'll be very hard training.

13:14.840 --> 13:17.150
I'm finished with the other libraries' requests.

13:17.150 --> 13:18.240
I see.

13:18.240 --> 13:20.650
Then, can you put back the returned books?

13:20.650 --> 13:21.590
Yes!

13:25.280 --> 13:28.140
Don't you think she's been getting better?

13:28.140 --> 13:30.870
That aside, what's up with her face?

13:30.920 --> 13:34.420
It seems it's because of the special training she's been doing every night.

13:34.420 --> 13:36.100
What the?

13:36.100 --> 13:39.460
No! 030 is an encyclopedia.

13:39.460 --> 13:43.350
They're big and heavy, so they're placed on the bottom shelves.

13:43.350 --> 13:45.310
Here you go.

13:46.290 --> 13:48.060
That's the 20th tonight!

13:48.060 --> 13:50.110
Look at all these pimples!

13:50.110 --> 13:52.730
It'll be seriously bad if I eat any more!

13:52.730 --> 13:55.610
It's because of the damage that you can get this desperate.

13:55.610 --> 13:56.440
Here.

13:59.030 --> 14:01.130
We'll work on request retrieval next.

14:01.990 --> 14:08.210
Speaking of retrieval, there have been so many missing books recently.

14:08.210 --> 14:10.910
Only this week, we already have 15.

14:10.910 --> 14:12.620
15?

14:12.620 --> 14:14.880
That's more than usual...

14:14.880 --> 14:16.480
You think so, too?

14:16.480 --> 14:17.880
Yeah...

14:23.030 --> 14:27.510
1098, 1098...

14:27.510 --> 14:30.240
1098 goes in hobbies shelf #126!

14:34.340 --> 14:36.680
Shouldn't you recognize her efforts already?

14:37.180 --> 14:40.450
She didn't do her best before.

14:40.450 --> 14:43.150
Isn't that called laziness?

14:44.550 --> 14:47.830
What do you want us to do with Kasahara?

14:48.370 --> 14:50.130
You argument is correct.

14:50.130 --> 14:53.120
However, the one who turns that argument into a weapon is wrong.

14:53.580 --> 14:55.070
Which one are you?

14:55.740 --> 14:57.920
Why don't you trust her a little?

14:58.400 --> 15:00.150
I'm sure there's something you can gain from her, too.

15:02.690 --> 15:05.800
15 missing books...

15:05.800 --> 15:11.470
There's usually some kind of scheme behind abnormal events...

15:13.780 --> 15:16.390
The Committee for the Deliberation of Questionable Books?

15:20.090 --> 15:21.360
These are...

15:23.220 --> 15:25.210
Those books are in the Chief Librarian's office.

15:25.210 --> 15:26.880
In the Chief Librarian's office?

15:26.880 --> 15:30.960
The Committee people are coming today.

15:30.960 --> 15:33.040
They want to discuss them while reading through the actual books.

15:33.040 --> 15:35.460
They wanted to gather the back-up copies, too?

15:35.460 --> 15:37.170
It's what they requested.

15:37.170 --> 15:38.890
Geez, I don't know what they're thinking.

15:42.810 --> 15:44.960
Incoming transmission from a patrolling officer!

15:44.960 --> 15:47.900
The Media Cleansing Force is surrounding the library!

15:47.900 --> 15:48.700
Wh-What?!

15:48.320 --> 15:51.070
All personnel, report immediately to your battle positions.

15:48.700 --> 15:49.980
It's a special call-up!

15:49.980 --> 15:51.070
Hurry!

15:51.570 --> 15:55.860
All users in the library should immediately evacuate the facility.

15:55.860 --> 15:57.010
Repeating.

15:57.010 --> 16:01.160
All users in the library should immediately evacuate the facility.

15:57.490 --> 15:59.200
Lock all the terminals!

16:01.720 --> 16:03.950
Close the underground book vault!

16:07.760 --> 16:08.920
They're going up?

16:08.920 --> 16:09.540
Why?

16:10.060 --> 16:13.750
Aren't they after the reading room or the underground book vault?

16:18.680 --> 16:22.060
They must have teamed up with the Committee for the Deliberation of Questionable Books,

16:22.060 --> 16:25.110
and are trying to confiscate all the books in the Chief Librarian's office.

16:25.770 --> 16:29.480
There were censored books amongst the list of problematic books!

16:30.940 --> 16:33.190
An emergency call from Administration!

16:33.190 --> 16:35.780
They're not after the underground book vault!

16:35.780 --> 16:37.990
They're really after the Chief Librarian's office!

16:39.780 --> 16:41.950
Hey! Where are you going?!

16:41.950 --> 16:43.700
You're going against orders!

16:43.700 --> 16:46.520
Shibasaki says they're heading to the Chief Librarian's office!

16:46.520 --> 16:48.660
She doesn't say meaningless things!

16:48.660 --> 16:50.250
There are no grounds!

16:50.250 --> 16:52.430
I know this woman, Shibasaki!

16:52.430 --> 16:53.670
That's my ground!

16:58.780 --> 17:00.720
LFC Tezuka to LOSC Dojo!

17:00.720 --> 17:04.070
We are switching our location because of information gained from a library staff member.

17:04.070 --> 17:05.470
We are heading to the Chief Librarian's office.

17:08.750 --> 17:10.040
You open it.

17:24.870 --> 17:26.330
Get down!

17:30.930 --> 17:31.840
They took them!

17:33.840 --> 17:36.640
We'll get to the rooftop through the emergency staircase.

17:36.640 --> 17:37.920
Why the rooftop?

17:38.460 --> 17:41.340
One of the Cleansing Force members was carrying a climbing rope.

17:42.260 --> 17:45.140
They're trying to rappel down from there!

17:57.280 --> 17:59.070
D-Damn it!

18:00.390 --> 18:01.780
You...

18:06.500 --> 18:09.430
The duffel bag with the books is in the bushes in the back yard!

18:09.430 --> 18:11.110
Please, retrieve it immediately!

18:11.110 --> 18:15.000
No! It'll be too late if we wait for them!

18:15.000 --> 18:17.550
But there's no other way!

18:21.010 --> 18:21.930
I'll go down.

18:21.930 --> 18:23.520
Back me up.

18:23.520 --> 18:24.800
No!

18:24.800 --> 18:25.890
I'll go!

18:25.890 --> 18:28.100
You don't like high places, do you?

18:29.390 --> 18:32.980
I don't need you to worry about me!

18:32.980 --> 18:34.900
Enough already!

18:34.900 --> 18:37.530
Do you really have to be the best at everything?!

18:40.780 --> 18:43.370
Why don't you trust her a little?

18:44.350 --> 18:45.660
Use these.

18:47.000 --> 18:50.080
I'll reach the ground before you are out of rounds.

18:51.290 --> 18:52.750
All right.

18:52.750 --> 18:53.960
Give me a count!

18:53.960 --> 18:55.590
One.

18:55.920 --> 18:56.770
Two.

18:57.630 --> 18:58.780
Three!

19:15.980 --> 19:17.640
Now what?

19:17.640 --> 19:19.480
I wasn't thinking about the next step!

19:19.480 --> 19:21.360
I'll make another dash!

19:21.360 --> 19:22.580
You idiot!

19:22.580 --> 19:24.160
Stay right there!

19:30.160 --> 19:31.370
Idiot!

19:31.370 --> 19:34.740
Fix your bad habit of acting on impulse!

19:34.740 --> 19:36.800
Use your brains!

19:36.800 --> 19:40.000
The first thing out of your mouth are insults?!

19:41.780 --> 19:47.230
Please, don't ever think about dashing through gunfire without backup!

19:47.850 --> 19:51.140
Consider how I came here after receiving the call!

19:53.120 --> 19:54.320
Shoot...

19:54.870 --> 19:56.980
I made him really worried.

19:59.670 --> 20:01.390
I'm sorry.

20:02.810 --> 20:07.200
But the decision to go to the Chief Librarian's office was good.

20:07.200 --> 20:11.210
It went against orders, but in the end, we were able to protect the books.

20:11.670 --> 20:13.370
It was a flexible and appropriate decision.

20:13.890 --> 20:17.740
Did he just praise me?

20:19.510 --> 20:21.300
Get a good rest tonight.

20:23.290 --> 20:24.160
Yes, Sir.

20:30.180 --> 20:33.260
No library staff were seriously injured.

20:33.260 --> 20:37.730
Although the Cleansing Force member you shot was hurt pretty badly.

20:37.730 --> 20:40.240
It was a calculated shot, so he'll be fine.

20:41.450 --> 20:43.190
Anyway, thanks for helping me earlier.

20:43.190 --> 20:46.150
I was able to calmly climb down because you were backing me up.

20:48.700 --> 20:51.410
What's with the sulky face?

20:51.970 --> 20:54.410
Do you still have something against me?

20:54.870 --> 20:56.890
I have a proposal.

20:56.890 --> 20:58.760
A proposal?

21:00.670 --> 21:01.740
Do you...

21:02.820 --> 21:04.300
want to go out with me?

21:14.540 --> 21:17.880
nani ka ga kawaru kigashita

21:14.540 --> 21:17.880
I had a feeling something was about to change

21:17.880 --> 21:21.260
nani mo kawaranu asa ni

21:17.880 --> 21:21.260
on this very ordinary morning

21:21.260 --> 21:26.270
itsu mo yori sukoshi ii mezamedatta

21:21.260 --> 21:26.270
I woke up feeling a little better than usual

21:27.930 --> 21:34.610
hito sashiyubi de sashimesu no wa mirai

21:27.930 --> 21:34.610
My index finger points out to the future

21:34.610 --> 21:44.280
kimi no te no hira ga fureru tabi ni afuru omoi

21:34.610 --> 21:44.280
My thoughts overflow each time I touch your palm

21:44.730 --> 21:48.260
ch-ch-ch-changes saa kawatteku

21:44.730 --> 21:48.260
Changes, yeah. I'm changing.

21:48.260 --> 21:51.580
sayonara furui jibun

21:48.260 --> 21:51.580
Goodbye my old self

21:51.580 --> 21:58.110
shingenjitsu atarashii nani ka ga matteru

21:51.580 --> 21:58.110
There's something new awaiting me in the new reality

21:58.110 --> 22:01.850
ch-ch-ch-changes saa kawatteku

21:58.110 --> 22:01.850
Changes, yeah. I'm changing.

22:01.850 --> 22:05.080
ushinau mono mo aru

22:01.850 --> 22:05.080
There are things I'll lose too

22:05.080 --> 22:10.850
demo iindesu hitotsu unazuki kakedasu

22:05.080 --> 22:10.850
But that's okay, I'll just nod and keep running

22:10.850 --> 22:18.400
saa subete ga ima kawatteku subete ga hajimaru

22:10.850 --> 22:18.400
Yeah, everything is changing now, everything starts now

22:18.400 --> 22:28.690
shingenjitsu dare no mono demo nai atarashii jibun

22:18.400 --> 22:28.690
It's a new reality, my new self belongs to no one but me
